config BR2_PACKAGE_STYX_OV9282
	bool "styx-ov9282"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Styx's build of the ov9282 sensor driver (OV9281/OV9282/OV9782):
	  the image kernel's own driver plus a 1280x480 mode centred on the
	  array, which reads 40% fewer lines than 1280x800. Installed to
	  /lib/modules/<release>/updates/, where it takes precedence over the
	  kernel's own ov9282.ko; the kernel itself is not changed. For Styx
	  images only (images using libcamera keep the stock driver).

	  The build fails when the kernel's own ov9282.c is not the one the
	  Styx driver was made from (re-import it: kernel-modules/ov9282).

comment "styx-ov9282 needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
